    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Ray Cooke Auctioneers are delighted to present Calliaghstown Cottage, a beautifully restored and extended period residence that effortlessly combines timeless character with modern family living. Set on approximately 0.7 acres of beautifully landscaped mature gardens, this exceptional home offers privacy, charm and remarkable versatility in a peaceful countryside setting on the Dublin/Kildare border.\nLovingly renovated and thoughtfully extended over the years, the property successfully balances its rich heritage with contemporary family living, creating a truly unique home in one of South Dublin's most desirable rural settings.\n\nA Home Rich in History\nSteeped in local history, Calliaghstown Cottage dates back to 1847, when it was constructed as a cottage on the historic Johnstown Kennedy Estate during the Great Irish Famine. The property was originally occupied by the estate's blacksmith following the construction of the nearby forge in 1849, adding a fascinating chapter to its rich heritage.\nThe name Calliaghstown is derived from the Irish Baile na gCailleach, meaning 'Townland of the Witches,' reflecting the area's deep-rooted folklore and history. In 1984, a sympathetic second storey was added, transforming the original cottage into the spacious family home enjoyed today while carefully preserving its unique period character.\nThe cottage also enjoys a location of significant historical interest. Just across the nearby County Kildare border lies Cromwellstown Hill, where Oliver Cromwell is said to have camped before his march on Kilkenny. The surrounding area is equally rich in heritage, with the remains of a Romanesque church and the ruins of a medieval castle located in the neighbouring townland of Kilteel, all contributing to the unique sense of place that surrounds this remarkable home.\n\nAccommodation\nA welcoming entrance hall, complete with a solid-fuel stove, immediately sets the tone for this character-filled home. To one side lies an elegant sitting room featuring extensive built-in bookshelves and a striking marble fireplace with a solid-fuel stove, while a fourth bedroom is positioned opposite, providing flexible family accommodation for guests, growing families or those seeking a home office.\nA short flight of steps leads to the heart of the home—a spacious, light-filled open-plan kitchen and dining room. The kitchen is fitted with painted Shaker-style units, a Belfast sink and a Stanley range cooker, blending traditional craftsmanship with practical family living. Adjoining the kitchen is a utility room, which can also serve as a pantry, together with a cloakroom and shower room.\nThe dining area opens directly onto the gardens through French doors, creating the perfect space for indoor-outdoor entertaining. A second solid-fuel stove provides additional warmth and ambience during the colder months.\nThe upper floor comprises three generous double bedrooms, including a spacious principal bedroom suite. The two south-facing bedrooms enjoy dual-aspect windows that maximise natural light throughout the day, while the principal bedroom benefits from four skylights. Beautiful exposed timber floorboards further enhance the home's authentic country charm and period appeal.\n\nDetached Two-Storey Building\nOne of the property's most impressive features is the detached two-storey block-built building, offering exceptional flexibility and enormous potential. Subject to the necessary planning permission, it could provide an ideal home office, guest accommodation, artist's studio or additional living space.\nThe building benefits from running water, electricity, sewage connections and an EV charging point. The ground floor includes a WC and substantial storage space, currently utilised as a workshop, while the bright first floor offers a generous open-plan space ready to be transformed into a games room, gym, creative studio, home office or teenager's retreat.\n\nGardens\nThe gardens at Calliaghstown Cottage are undoubtedly one of its finest features. Extending to approximately 0.7 acres, they have been thoughtfully landscaped with mature trees, herbaceous borders and an abundance of seasonal planting, creating a private oasis that can be enjoyed throughout the year.\nA brick-paved driveway provides ample private parking, while a patio complete with a gazebo offers an inviting setting for outdoor dining and entertaining. A picturesque stream borders the garden and is accessed by a set of steps, providing a tranquil spot to relax, read or simply enjoy the peaceful surroundings.\nThe gardens feature an impressive variety of established planting, including lilies, lavender, delphiniums, phlox, lupins and peonies, ensuring colour and interest across the seasons.\nFor gardening enthusiasts, there is a greenhouse, a second vegetable greenhouse, a substantial steel garden shed with a cobbled floor and a separate timber potting shed, making this an exceptional property for those with a passion for gardening or self-sufficiency.\nAltogether, the gardens provide a peaceful sanctuary for nature lovers and those seeking the perfect balance between country living and convenient access to Dublin.\n\nServices\nOil-fired central heating via Stanley Range\nFibre broadband\nPrivate well water supply\nPrivate septic tank (Bord na Móna Puraflo system)\nProspective purchasers should satisfy themselves as to the availability and adequacy of all services.\n\nBER: C\nBER Number: 117444927\n\nLocation\nCalliaghstown Cottage enjoys an enviable location on the Dublin/Kildare border, offering the tranquillity of the countryside while benefiting from excellent connectivity via the N7 and M50.\nRathcoole, just 4 km away, provides an excellent range of everyday amenities, including supermarkets, cafés, restaurants and the ever-popular Avoca store and café.\nNaas, approximately 11 km from the property, offers an extensive selection of restaurants, cafés, supermarkets, boutiques and retail shopping, while Dublin City Centre is within easy commuting distance.\nThe area is renowned for its sporting and leisure amenities, with Punchestown Racecourse and Naas Racecourse both within 13 km. Golf enthusiasts are particularly well catered for, with Beech Park Golf Club (1 km), Citywest Golf Club (8 km) and the championship course at The K Club, Straffan (13 km) all nearby.\nFamilies are equally well served with an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area, together with convenient access to many of Dublin's leading schools.\n\nDistances\nRathcoole 4 km\nSaggart Luas Station 6 km\nNaas 11 km\nDublin City Centre 28 km\nDublin Airport 33 km\nViewing\n\nViewing is strictly by private appointment with Ray Cooke Auctioneers."
